Thank you to P. Burns, A. Liaw and R. Burbridge who answered.

#  I have some very large files on my .Data directory (Unix) that
start "___" e.g. "___6oe7". Can I safely get rid of
these?

The clue, provided by P. Burns, is in S Poetry (see web references
below).  Here is his answer.

Those files are supposed to be for objects 

whose name is troublesome as a file name in the operating system. 

Look at __nonfile to see if those files are referenced. Some times 

these files are created (and can be large) when S goes a little 

wobbly in the head.

Since I was careful to use proper names, there is no ___nonfile, and
ls() brings up the same list of files whether or not the ___ files are in
.Data, I presume that I am in the "wobbly" area.  Just to
be safe, they are going onto a storage tape until the study is
completed.   

