Try this:

> all(is.na(test))

  That should return T if all elements are NA.  Also, consider the
following:

> test1 <- rep(c(1,NA), c(10,10))
> test2 <- rep(NA, 20)
> test3 <- rep(1, 20)
> all(is.na(test1))
[1] F
> all(is.na(test2))
[1] T
> all(is.na(test3))
[1] F
> any(is.na(test1))
[1] T
> any(is.na(test2))
[1] T
> any(is.na(test3))
[1] F

Hope this helps,

Chuck Cleland

